"  bladecp partner vibe create
 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Creates the BladeCP Vibe account of one of your services, the same call the
  BladeCP WHMCS module makes. One account per service: when the service already
  has one, the API returns it and creates nothing.

  Usage ──────────────────────────────────────
  bladecp partner vibe create --external-id <id> --plan <id> --email <email>
      --name <name> [--email-verification <verified|not-required>] [--yes]

  Options ────────────────────────────────────
  --external-id <id>                             Your ID for the service (for
                                                 example the WHMCS service ID)
  --plan <id>                                    UUID of the Vibe plan (see
                                                 "bladecp partner plans")
  --email <email>                                Email of the account owner
  --name <name>                                  Name of the account owner
  --email-verification <verified|not-required>   Free plans: the owner's email
                                                 was verified, or your store
                                                 does not require it
  -y, --yes                                      Do not ask for confirmation on
                                                 a terminal

  --plan takes the UUID of one of your Vibe plans; "bladecp partner plans"
  lists them.
  Free plans need --email-verification: you state, as the WHMCS module does,
  that the owner's email was verified (verified) or that your store does not
  require it (not-required). The CLI sends that statement with the current
  time.
