"  bladecp partner vibe create
 ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Creates the BladeCP Vibe account of one of your services, the same call the BladeCP WHMCS module
  makes. One account per service: when the service already has one, the API returns it and creates
  nothing.

  Usage ──────────────────────────────────────
  bladecp partner vibe create --external-id <id> --plan <id> --email <email> --name <name>
      [--email-verification <verified|not-required>] [--yes]

  Options ────────────────────────────────────
  --external-id <id>                             Your ID for the service (for example the WHMCS
                                                 service ID)
  --plan <id>                                    UUID of the Vibe plan (see "bladecp partner
                                                 plans")
  --email <email>                                Email of the account owner
  --name <name>                                  Name of the account owner
  --email-verification <verified|not-required>   Free plans: the owner's email was verified, or
                                                 your store does not require it
  -y, --yes                                      Do not ask for confirmation on a terminal

  --plan takes the UUID of one of your Vibe plans; "bladecp partner plans" lists them.
  Free plans need --email-verification: you state, as the WHMCS module does, that the owner's email
  was verified (verified) or that your store does not require it (not-required). The CLI sends that
  statement with the current time.
  When BladeCP requires a linked identity for new accounts, the API refuses with
  identity_link_required. The account is then created by the identity link of the WHMCS module,
  which the customer completes in the browser.
  On a terminal it asks first (Enter creates); --yes skips the question. Trying again never creates
  a second account.

  Examples ───────────────────────────────────
  › bladecp partner vibe create --external-id 4821 --plan <plan-uuid> --email owner@example.com --name "Store Owner"
    Create the account of a service on a Pro plan
  › bladecp partner vibe create --external-id 4822 --plan <plan-uuid> --email owner@example.com --name "Store Owner"
    --email-verification verified
    On a Free plan, with the owner email already verified

  Global options ─────────────────────────────
  --json                 Print machine-readable JSON (no colors, no prompts)
  --api-url <url>        API address (default https://api.bladecp.com)
  --lang <en|pt-BR|es>   Language for messages
  --debug                Describe each request on stderr (the key is never shown)
  --verbose              Same as --debug
  -h, --help             Show help
  -v, --version          Show the version

